    "title": "What channel is Nebraska vs Iowa college football game today? Start time, TV schedule, streaming",
    "text": "Nov. 28, 2025, 9:30 a.m. ETNebraska football will look to bounce back in Week 14 after an underwhelming performance at Penn State.To do that, Matt Rhule's Cornhuskers will have to take down one of their Big Ten foes in Iowa.Stream Nebraska vs. Iowa football live with Fubo (free trial)Nebraska and Iowa are slated for a 15th consecutive Black Friday meeting for their annual \"Heroes Game\" trophy, which has gone to the Hawkeyes in each of the last two seasons.The Cornhuskers are coming off a 37-10 loss at Penn State in Week 13. Backup quarterback TJ Lateef, who has started the last two games for the injured Dylan Raiola, completed 21 of 37 passes for 187 yards and had Nebraska's lone touchdown score of the game, an 11-yard run in the third quarter.Nebraska enters Friday's rivalry game with a 30-22-3 edge in the all-time series against Iowa, though the Hawkeyes lead the rivalry series 10-4 since the Cornhuskers joined the Big Ten. The Cornhuskers also have a 10-8 record when playing at home on Black Friday since 1990.Here's how to watch the Week 14 game between Nebraska and Iowa, including time, TV schedule, streaming info, game odds and more:What TV channel is Nebraska vs Iowa football on today?TV channel: CBSStreaming:Paramount+ | Fubo (free trial)Nebraska will take on Iowa on CBS with Rich Waltz, Ross Tucker and Tiffany Blackman on the call. Streaming options for the game include Paramount+, CBS's subscription streaming service, and Fubo, which includes CBS and offers a free trial to new subscribers.Nebraska vs Iowa football time todayDate: Friday, Nov. 28Time: Noon ET | 11 a.m. CTLocation: Memorial Stadium (Lincoln, Neb.)The Cornhuskers and the Hawkeyes are scheduled to kick off from Memorial Stadium in Lincoln, Nebraska at noon ET (11 a.m. CT).Nebraska vs Iowa football predictions, picks, oddsOdds courtesy of BetMGM as of Tuesday, Nov. 25Spread: Iowa -6Over/under: 38.5Moneyline: Iowa (-235) | Nebraska (+195)Prediction (Chad Leistikow, The Des Moines Register/Hawk Central): Iowa 27, Nebraska 16 \"... Iowa showed up ready to play in its last two road games, blasting Wisconsin (37-0) and leading USC, 21-7. The Hawkeyes take an early lead behind a Gronowski rushing TD, and Kamari Moulton tops 100 yards rushing for the first time this season. The defense will force one major turnover and make this the first Iowa-Nebraska game decided by more than seven points since 2017.\"Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.Gambling involves risk. Please only gamble with funds that you can comfortably afford to lose. While we do our utmost to offer good advice and information we cannot be held responsible for any loss that may be incurred as a result of gambling. We do our best to make sure all the information that we provide on this site is correct. However, from time to time mistakes will be made and we will not be held liable. Please check any stats or information if you are unsure how accurate they are. No guarantees are made with regards to results or financial gain. All forms of betting carry financial risk and it is up to the individual to make bets with or without the assistance of information provided on this site and we cannot be held responsible for any loss that may be incurred as a result of following the betting tips provided on this site. Past performances do not guarantee success in the future and betting odds fluctuate from one minute to the next. The material contained on this site is intended to inform, entertain and educate the reader and in no way represents an inducement to gamble legally or illegally or any sort of professional advice.Gannett may earn revenue from sports betting operators for audience referrals to betting services. Sports betting operators have no influence over nor are any such revenues in any way dependent on or linke